# Copy to .env.local and fill in — see the Self-Hosting Guide in README.md.
#
# All four are PUBLISHABLE client-side keys: they are compiled into the
# JavaScript bundle and are visible to anyone using the app. Safety comes from
# Row Level Security (Supabase) and from key restrictions (Mapbox/Google), not
# from keeping these secret. Never put a Supabase service-role key here — that
# one is a real secret and belongs only in Edge Function secrets.
#
# .env.local is gitignored. This file is the template; keep it free of real values.

# Supabase → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# Mapbox → the URL-RESTRICTED browser token (step 4 of the guide).
# The separate unrestricted token belongs in the MAPBOX_TOKEN function secret.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=pk.eyJ...

# Google Cloud → Maps JavaScript API + Places API, restricted to your domains
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=AIza...
